REQ-ZRM-BASE
When the analysis dictionary contains a configuration block derived from ZermeloTrjGen, the program shall execute a route-generation workflow.
The workflow shall:
-validate common route-generation configuration;
-define the route space;
-determine route start locations;
-determine route destination locations;
-prepare route obstacles;
-invoke a route-construction strategy;
-compute route metrics;
-collect route results;
-record unreachable starts;
-provide route results to a route writer.
Implementation
ZermeloTrjGen shall:
-own common configuration parsing and validation;
-determine the route space from the common height-range settings;
-read startPatches, destinationPatches, and obstaclePatches;
-use ground as the default value for obstaclePatches;
-allow an optional non-negative deviceRadius, defaulting to zero;
-allow an optional non-negative obstacleMargin, defaulting to zero;
-require a positive deviceSpeed when specified;
-use 0.1 m/s as the default deviceSpeed;
-compute intersections between the route space and the configured start, destination, and obstacle patches;
-sample nPoints start locations from the start-patch intersections using segment-length weighting;
-prepare obstacle representations expanded by deviceRadius + obstacleMargin;
-select, for each start location, a destination location according to the generator strategy;
-invoke a derived-class route-construction strategy for each start location;
-compute route length from the route geometry returned by the derived strategy;
-compute travel time from route length and deviceSpeed;
-collect successful route results;
-record unreachable start locations;
-provide generated routes and associated metadata to the configured route writer.
If variableHeight is enabled and the selected generator does not support variable-height routing, the program shall terminate with a configuration error.
Related class
ZermeloTrjGen

REQ-ZRM-NOFLOW
When the analysis dictionary contains a ZermeloTrjNoFlow block, the program shall generate routes without using flow-field information.
The generated route shall not depend on velocity, pressure, turbulence, or any other flow-field quantity.
Implementation
ZermeloTrjNoFlow shall:
-derive from ZermeloTrjGen;
-generate routes in a horizontal plane located at the midpoint of minHeight and maxHeight;
-use the start locations, destination locations, and obstacle representations prepared by ZermeloTrjGen;
-construct a visibility graph using route endpoints and obstacle geometry;
-determine the shortest collision-free piecewise-linear route between a start location and the selected destination location;
-ensure that no route segment intersects an expanded obstacle;
-return the route geometry to the base workflow for result processing;
-report the route as unreachable when no collision-free path exists.
Variable-height routing is outside the scope of this generator. If variableHeight is enabled, the generator shall terminate with a configuration error.
Related class
ZermeloTrjNoFlow : public ZermeloTrjGen

REQ-NOFLOW-ZRM-ROUTE
For each sampled start location, the program shall generate a collision-free route to the selected destination location.
If no feasible route exists, the start location shall be reported as unreachable.
Implementation
For each sampled start location:
-the generator shall use the fixed-height route plane defined by the base workflow;
-the generator shall use the expanded obstacle footprints prepared by the base workflow;
-the generator shall construct a visibility graph from obstacle vertices and route endpoints;
-the generator shall determine the shortest collision-free piecewise-linear route from the start location to the selected destination location;
-route segments shall not intersect expanded obstacle footprints;
if no collision-free route exists, the generator shall report the start location as unreachable and shall not generate route geometry for that start.
The route-generation algorithm shall be purely geometric and shall not depend on any flow-field quantity.
Related class
ZermeloTrjNoFlow

REQ-NOFLOW-ZRM-OUTPUT
The program shall write Zermelo route results separately from streamline results.
Implementation
For each successful route, the output shall contain:
-a stable route identifier;
-start coordinates;
-end coordinates;
-route waypoints;
-route length;
-travel time.
For each unreachable start location, the output shall record the unreachable condition.
Route output shall be produced through a dedicated Zermelo route writer.
Related class
ZermeloRouteWriter